body:
`admin_events` has carried `resolved`/`resolved_at`/`resolved_by` since it was created, and the admin surface **reads all three**. The fingerprint detail page even has an empty state reading *"Either every event has been resolved or this fingerprint no longer matches any admin_events row."*

**Nothing in the product could ever write them.** There is no resolve action anywhere in `src/`, so every error ever logged stays unresolved forever — and a defect fixed and deployed weeks ago sits in the dashboard beside one that broke five minutes ago, indistinguishable.

That is not cosmetic, and it has already cost us. It is exactly why the Stripe webhook failure went unnoticed for three days: it logged at `error` into a channel nobody could trust, because the channel could not tell *"still broken"* from *"nobody ever closed it"*. Triaging the seven unresolved clusters on 2026-08-09 required reading the source and diffing it against the running commit to discover that two of them — the class-sync timestamp crash and the onboarding avatar upload — were **already fixed and deployed**.

Scoped deliberately narrowly:
- super-admin gated on the **first line**, same gate as every other admin write;
- resolves **one** fingerprint, never a bulk sweep;
- filters to rows already unresolved, so a re-run cannot overwrite who resolved what or when;
- records **who**, because "resolved" with no name is the same unfalsifiable claim this exists to remove;
- reports 0 as *"already resolved"* rather than as either a failure or a fabricated success;
- reads the write's `error` and refuses instead of claiming success.

Verified: 6 tests — happy path, open-rows-only filter, already-resolved no-op, super-admin gate, failed write, empty fingerprint; lint 0; tsc 0; full suite 996 files / 9297 passed.

## Root cause

`src/app/baseball/actions/messages.ts` is a `'use server'` actions barrel file that re-exported `sendBaseballMessage`, `createBaseballConversation`, and `markBaseballMessagesAsRead` (from `@/app/actions/messages`) via a plain renaming re-export:

```ts
export {
  sendBaseballMessage as sendMessage,
  createBaseballConversation as createConversation,
  markBaseballMessagesAsRead as markMessagesAsRead,
} from '@/app/actions/messages';
```

Next.js 16 requires every top-level export of a file carrying the `'use server'` directive to be declared **directly in that file** as an async function. A pass-through `export { x as y } from '...'` re-export does not satisfy that shape (it's a non-async export as far as the Next compiler's server-action codemod is concerned), so `next build` fails as soon as anything imports the module.

This is exactly the kind of defect `tsc --noEmit` can't catch (TypeScript has no opinion on the `'use server'` directive/build-plugin contract), which is why it type-checked clean while breaking the actual Next build. The barrel already has 4 real importers today (`messages/page.tsx`, `PlayerDetailModal.tsx`, `use-messages.ts`, and the `use-messages` test's module mock), and `PlayerProfileCoachActions.tsx` on #662 adds a 5th client-side import (`createConversation`) — so this trips the moment #662 lands.

## Fix

Replaced the barrel re-export with three async wrapper functions that call straight through to the originals with **identical parameter and return shapes**:

```ts
export async function sendMessage(conversationId: string, content: string) {
  return sendBaseballMessage(conversationId, content);
}

export async function createConversation(participantUserIds: string[]) {
  return createBaseballConversation(participantUserIds);
}

export async function markMessagesAsRead(conversationId: string) {
  return markBaseballMessagesAsRead(conversationId);
}
```

Each export is now a directly-declared async function, satisfying the `'use server'` file contract, while preserving the exact public API (`sendMessage`, `createConversation`, `markMessagesAsRead`) and call shape every existing importer already relies on.

`getPlayerUserId` is not present on this branch's copy of the file (it's added separately by the in-flight #657 Discover-peek PR) — nothing here touches it.

## Verification

- Grepped every importer of `@/app/baseball/actions/messages` (`messages/page.tsx`, `PlayerDetailModal.tsx`, `use-messages.ts`, `use-messages.test.tsx`) — all call sites match the wrapper signatures unchanged.
- `npx eslint src/app/baseball/actions/messages.ts` → 0 errors, 0 warnings.
- `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` (full project) → 0 errors.
- `npx vitest run src/hooks/__tests__/use-messages.test.tsx` → 28/28 passed.
- `npx next build --experimental-build-mode compile` was attempted but hit an unrelated Turbopack/symlink environment error in this worktree setup (`Symlink [project]/node_modules is invalid, it points out of the filesystem root`) before reaching any type-checking — the integrator's full `next build` should be used as the final gate for the Next-compiler-specific `'use server'` export-shape check.

